+//   F3  the marker table refuses a pattern over 50 bytes, under 3, or made only of wildcards, on INSERT and UPDATE; a hard row is not changed or deleted
+//       without ops_config default_approve_marker_edit; the old table refuses an INSERT with a pointer; the marker-health detector reads 0 and fails
+//   F1  33 adversarial money, signing, deletion, owner-name, account, credential, privacy and suppression cards in three shapes, 35 punctuation and spacing
+//       variants, and a probe sentence for every hard marker are never approved; a hard marker found only in the title, only in the action, as the first word
+//       is hard, one found only in the stated default is not; the reversible false-positive cards (model ids, package scopes, a cache key, ...) stay approvable
+//   F2  a hard card is only excluded from the approve wording: it keeps the old reroute (the autonomy trigger has no hard condition)
+//   F4  the queue description puts the code-task: line on a line of its own (the code loop's INTAKE_MARK matches it)
+//   F5/F11 the records; F6 one switch (autonomy_first_gate) stops both paths; F8 decision detection; F9 the detectors are executed, the fail-closed gate,
